  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Given that $x=\\dfrac{2}{3\\sqrt2-1}$, find the value of each expression, giving answers in simplest form with a rational denominator.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p20-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{4(19+6\\sqrt2)}{289}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{2(3\\sqrt2+1)}{(3\\sqrt2-1)(3\\sqrt2+1)}\\\\x&=\\frac{2(3\\sqrt2+1)}{17}\\\\x^2&=\\frac{4(3\\sqrt2+1)^2}{289}\\\\x^2&=\\frac{4(18+6\\sqrt2+1)}{289}\\\\x^2&=\\frac{4(19+6\\sqrt2)}{289}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{3\\sqrt2-1}{2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1x&=1\\div\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt2-1}\\\\\\frac1x&=\\frac{3\\sqrt2-1}{2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q8-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{x^2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{19-6\\sqrt2}{4}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1{x^2}&=\\left(\\frac{3\\sqrt2-1}{2}\\right)^2\\\\\\frac1{x^2}&=\\frac{18-6\\sqrt2+1}{4}\\\\\\frac1{x^2}&=\\frac{19-6\\sqrt2}{4}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q8-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$x+\\dfrac{1}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{63\\sqrt2-13}{34}$\n\nRationalise $x$, then use a common denominator.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x+\\frac1x&=\\frac{6\\sqrt2+2}{17}+\\frac{3\\sqrt2-1}{2}\\\\x+\\frac1x&=\\frac{12\\sqrt2+4+51\\sqrt2-17}{34}\\\\x+\\frac1x&=\\frac{63\\sqrt2-13}{34}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q8-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$x^2+\\dfrac{1}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{915\\sqrt2-137}{578}$\n\nUse the results for $x^2$ and $\\frac{1}{x}$ with a common denominator.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+\\frac1x&=\\frac{4(19+6\\sqrt2)}{289}+\\frac{3\\sqrt2-1}{2}\\\\x^2+\\frac1x&=\\frac{8(19+6\\sqrt2)+289(3\\sqrt2-1)}{578}\\\\x^2+\\frac1x&=\\frac{152+48\\sqrt2+867\\sqrt2-289}{578}\\\\x^2+\\frac1x&=\\frac{915\\sqrt2-137}{578}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q8-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$x^2+\\dfrac{1}{x^2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{5795-1638\\sqrt2}{1156}$\n\nUse the results for $x^2$ and $\\frac{1}{x^2}$ with a common denominator.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+\\frac1{x^2}&=\\frac{4(19+6\\sqrt2)}{289}+\\frac{19-6\\sqrt2}{4}\\\\x^2+\\frac1{x^2}&=\\frac{16(19+6\\sqrt2)+289(19-6\\sqrt2)}{1156}\\\\x^2+\\frac1{x^2}&=\\frac{304+96\\sqrt2+5491-1734\\sqrt2}{1156}\\\\x^2+\\frac1{x^2}&=\\frac{5795-1638\\sqrt2}{1156}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
    ]
  },
